{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1568390388,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0OTM0MDI3NjM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3669","origin":"github"},"title":"[wishlist] datalad restore","message":"In the world of \"I use datalad alone\" (no direct git/git-annex), we might need a command which would be likely just calling `git reset --hard [state]` but also (relates to our \"states\"/branches manipulation issue TODO to find/link) eventually handle submodules correctly.\n\nThe rationale is that `datalad` philosophy is to go between clean/saved states of the dataset.  But our commands can fail leaving repository in a not clean state. E.g. in our with @dnkennedy exploration of `datalad run` output was unlocked, but then command failed, and we were left with unlocked files on the drive preventing us to do any other `run`.  Resetting state to the prior clean state is the reasonable way to deal with such issues in a general systematic way.","files":null}]}